BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Family Fun Fall Night\, McCormick's Creek State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261023T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261023T210000
UID:b7623343186cffb36d4cb24725a589e0@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, October 23 rd Family Fun Fall Night 4 pm: Leaf Poundi
 ng Bandana- (Craft) Trees are getting ready to store their energy from the
 ir leaves into their trunks. Come to the Nature Center to hammer the color
 s of the forest into a bandana to take home. Learn how leaves are changing
  and preserve them on a wearable art. The cost of this program $3 per band
 ana. Program is held at Nature Center Amphitheater . 5 pm-6:30 pm: Face Pa
 inting- Come get a spooky new face before tonight&rsquo\;s Halloween movie
  showing. Free face painting is being offered at the Canyon Inn. 5 pm-6:30
 pm: Book Mobile- Owen County Book Mobile will be making a surprise stop at
  McCormick&rsquo\;s Creek. Come check out the book mobile and create a spo
 oky craft in front of the Canyon Inn. 6:30 pm: Spooky Movie Night- Come se
 e a spooky family-friendly movie showing on the big screen in the Lobby at
  the Canyon Inn. Enjoy free popcorn and cookies. This movie is rated G for
  everyone. 8 pm: Owl Prowl- Join a Park Naturalist in front of the Canyon 
 Inn to learn about owl adaptations and call-in owls on this 1.4 mile night
  hike through the woods! Bring a redlight flashlight or borrow one from th
 e naturalist.
LOCATION:McCormick's Creek State Park\, 250 McCormick's Creek Park Road\, 
 Spencer\, IN 47460
URL:on.IN.gov/mccormickscreek
X-SOURCE:McCormick's Creek State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Falloween\, McCormick's Creek State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T000000
UID:604e73741b2f96599ecddee6c168b990@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, October 24 th Fall-o-ween 9:30 am-12 pm: Buck&rsquo
 \;s Dead and Breakfast- Come create a spooky sweet treat at Buck&rsquo\;s 
 Dead and Breakfast found in the Nature Center parking lot. Please bring ca
 sh\, all proceeds go to Friends of McCormick&rsquo\;s Creek. Create a Spid
 er Donuts $5. Hot Drinks $2. 10 am-12 pm: Pumpkin Carving- Carve a pumpkin
  and support the Friends of McCormick&rsquo\;s Creek. $5 cost per pumpkin.
  Please pay in cash and supplies are limited to the first 50 guests. Meet 
 at the Nature Center Amphitheater to begin. 3 pm-4 pm- Ssssnakes- (Live An
 imals) Slither on over to our Nature Center Amphitheater to learn about th
 e longest snake of North America and the strongest predatory snake in Indi
 ana. Naturalist Kaitlyn will introduce you to our snake ambassadors in thi
 s live animal program. 5:30 pm- 7:30 pm: Pumpkin Parade - (Hike) Put on a 
 costume and meet the Friends of McCormick&rsquo\;s Creek at the Nature Cen
 ter to take a spooky hike through the woods to see Jack-o-Lanterns from lo
 cal artists. We will be on an accessible path for everyone to enjoy. Vote 
 on your favorite Jack-o-Lanterns and take a treat bag to go! 8 pm-9 pm: No
 cturnal Animal Show- (Live Animals) Come join WildCare to meet some of the
 ir nocturnal animal ambassadors\, Silver Haired Bat and Southern Flying Sq
 uirrel. Discover the difference in these flying mammals! Program is being 
 offered at the Nature Center Audiotorium.&nbsp\;
LOCATION:McCormick's Creek State Park\, Nature Center\, 250 McCormick's Cr
 eek Park Road\, Spencer\, IN 47460
URL:on.in.gov/mccormickscreek
X-SOURCE:McCormick's Creek State Park
END:VEVENT
